  "worked_solution": "Let $x$ be the total number of participants.\n\nWe're told that $60%$ of participants enjoy painting. Thus, the number of participants who enjoy painting is $0.6x.$\n\nWe are also told that of those participants, $25%$ preferred landscapes. So, the number of participants who preferred landscape painting is\n\n$$\n0.25(0.6x)=0.15x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.15x$ represents $15%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $15%$ of all participants preferred landscape painting.",
